This directory contains a couple of updates to VM370CE that
go along with the Print/Punch File Handshake modification
to Hercules. Specifically, when these updates are applied
to the CP component of VM370CE v1.1.2, you will be able to
utilize the new Hercules "handshake" option for printer and 
punch devices.

There are three updates that need to be applied to CP:

* HRC242DK - allows program control of Command-Reject error
             handling. The next update uses this to prevent
             I/O errors being posted when the Hercules
             "handshake" option is not in force.

* HRC243DK - adds a new entry point (DMKIOSYN) that allows
             I/O to be processed synchronously without the 
             need to create a "completion handler" and 
             make a trip thru to dispatcher.   

* HRC244DK - updates the spooled print/punch processing to
             utilize the new File-Open/Close CCWs to create
             individual native files for each VM spool file.
             This update also makes a change to punch file
             handling under Hercules by bypassing the IntReq
             step that is part of the standard VM processing.
                 